# Overlay primitives

Read [docs/UI.md](docs/UI.md) before nesting a menu in a dialog or adding a z-index.

- Three mutually exclusive choices → `Segmented` in `ui.tsx`, not `Select`.
- Page menus `.menu` = `z-50`. Dialogs = `z-[70]`/`z-[71]`. Menus over a dialog = `z-[80]`. Command palette = `z-[85]`/`z-[86]`. Do not invent `z-[9999]`.
- Select/Combobox already portal and set `z-[80]`. A new portaled menu that can open over `Modal` must too, plus `pointer-events-auto` if clicks miss.
- `Modal` treats a click on `.menu` as inside the dialog. Keep that if you add another portaled overlay.
- Select uses `position="popper"` on purpose (`item-aligned` breaks in `overflow-hidden`).
- `overflow-hidden` / `transform` / `opacity-<100` clip or trap stacking. Portal out; do not raise z-index on the clipped child.
- Cap `ScrollArea` height on the ScrollArea, never with native `overflow-auto` on a wrapper that contains a menu.
